  "final": "Both `get_document` and `list_documents` now only return documents that match the given tenant and owner and have `deleted_at IS NULL`. The public check and a new access check both pass.\n\n**Changes**\n\n- **`src/repository.py`**\n  - `find(connection, tenant, owner, document_id)` filters on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND id=? AND deleted_at IS NULL`. It returns `None` for a missing, deleted, cross-tenant or cross-owner record, so the caller can't tell them apart.\n  - `listing(connection, tenant, owner)` filters on `tenant=? AND owner=? AND deleted_at IS NULL ORDER BY id`.\n  - All values are bound parameters, so names with quotes or SQL-like text are treated as literal values.\n  - `decode` is unchanged, so results still contain only `id`, `title` and `body`.\n- **`src/service.py`**: `get_document` and `list_documents` pass `tenant` and `owner` through. Previously they ignored both.\n- **`checks/access_checks.py`** (new): covers accessible and unavailable records, quoted tenant and owner names, injection-style input, list ordering, and the exact result keys.\n\n**Verification**\n\n- `python3 checks/public.py` passes before and after the change.\n- `python3 checks/access_checks.py` passes.\n\nThe `find` and `listing` signatures changed. `service.py` is their only caller, so nothing else needed updating. I didn't change the `document_id` handling or the schema.",
